{
 "check": "EPA cycles vs EPA test-car list (MY2022-2024)",
 "n_vehicles": 47,
 "n_by_arch": {
  "bev": 11,
  "conv": 22,
  "hev_parallel_p2": 6,
  "hev_powersplit": 6,
  "hev_series": 2
 },
 "method": "Check: EPA cycles (FTP-75 / HWFET / US06, plus SC03 and the 20 F cold FTP where tested) for 47 real MY2022-24\ntest vehicles (22 conventional, 14 HEV, 11 BEV) vs their EPA test-car-list results.  Writes cycles_vs_epa.json.\n\nError = simulated / EPA - 1 on fuel economy (mpg, or MPGe; for BEVs reported in kWh/100 mi the error is on\n1/consumption, i.e. also an 'economy' error).  Calibrated constants were fitted on the dev subset only; the headline\nnumbers are the held-out vehicles.",
 "procedures": "Emulate EPA chassis-dynamometer procedures with roadsim.\n\nFTP-75: cold-start UDDS (bags 1+2) after a soak at 24 C, 10-minute hot soak, hot-start bag 3 (first 505 s of UDDS).\n        FE = 1 / (0.43 (g1+g2)/(d1+d2) + 0.57 (g3+g2)/(d3+d2))  [40 CFR 600.113]\nHWFET, US06: hot start (preceded by a preconditioning run).\nHybrids: test starts at the SOC reached after preconditioning runs; residual net battery energy converted to fuel with a\n          fixed 1/(0.33 x 0.90) equivalence (SAE J1711-style correction).\nBEV: DC battery energy over a warm cycle, divided by an assumed 0.88 wall-to-battery charging efficiency to compare\n     with EPA's AC recharge energy (SAE J1634).  HVAC off for FTP/HWFET/US06 (as on the test).",
 "calibration": {
  "cold_fric_gasoline": 45.27,
  "cold_fric_diesel": 45.27,
  "cat_warmup_s": 10.0,
  "motor_loss_scale": 1.0,
  "bev_motor_loss_scale": 0.472,
  "cold_fric_hybrid_factor": 0.158
 },
